{
  "_comment": "Footprint mass table for SI placement dynamics (branch: feature/si-dynamics). Masses in grams. ALL mass_g values are rough guesses from datasheet/package norms, good enough to give inertia the right order of magnitude — scripts/calibrate_si.py fits the dynamics around them, not the reverse. Add rows for your own libraries; loader resolution: exact footprint_id first, then first case-insensitive keyword substring match (specific entries MUST precede general ones), then area fallback m = density*area + floor. Effective mass is always clamped to >= mass_floor_g so F=ma can never divide by zero.",
